# PR#45: this is the reverse of what round 6 of the same review asked for, and the
# invariant it cites does not say what it is read as saying. Invariant 5 is that a
# redelivered command must not duplicate a side effect. `presence.set` and
# `presence.subscribe` do not have one to duplicate: the second application leaves
# WhatsApp in the state the first one did -- available is available, subscribed is
# subscribed -- so repeating them is not a second effect, it is the same effect asserted
# again. A send is the shape the invariant is about, and it is in the ledger.
#
# What the exclusion buys is the failure that is not recoverable. Availability and every
# subscription belong to the socket that set them; WhatsApp forgets both when the
# connection goes and whatsmeow replays neither. A redelivery answered from the ledger
# reports success over a connection where nothing was done, and nothing after that ever
# corrects it -- there is no second chance the way a dropped receipt has one. Between an
# operation applied twice to the same end and one reported as applied and never applied,
# the second is the one worth avoiding.
#
# The remedy proposed instead -- replay the desired presence when a new socket connects --
# is the better design and a larger one, and it fixes something this does not: presence is
# lost on any ordinary reconnect, redelivery or no. That is registered as its own issue
# rather than folded in here, because the subscription set it would have to keep is
# unbounded by construction and deciding how to bound it is not this slice's decision.
# Registered as #46.
